WEBVTT


00:03:19.581 --> 00:03:21.617
- Go, Green!
- Boo!


00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:32.648
Come on, Eagles! You're killing me.
Show some pride out there.


00:03:32.886 --> 00:03:35.081
Some pride?
What are you talking about?


00:03:35.264 --> 00:03:36.697
These guys lost their pride
two months ago.


00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:37.998
What're you doing? Over!


00:03:38.142 --> 00:03:40.781
- They're still our boys, Tommy.
- Not this year, pally.


00:03:40.978 --> 00:03:43.412
Not in this town. Not in this town!


00:03:43.605 --> 00:03:45.561
- Stupid...
- You stink!


00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.269
Come on! Come on! Come on!


00:03:48.444 --> 00:03:49.513
Ball down.


00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.854
Hey, way to pack it in, Eagles!
You're quitters!


00:03:53.073 --> 00:03:56.827
31-0 to a team
should've been worse than us!


00:03:57.995 --> 00:03:59.587
What a bunch of losers!


00:04:01.081 --> 00:04:03.549
Hey! Hey!
Where do you think you's going, huh?


00:04:03.751 --> 00:04:05.184
Game's not over yet.


00:04:05.794 --> 00:04:07.830
Get back down to your seats, there.


00:04:11.258 --> 00:04:12.452
Believe this?


00:04:14.011 --> 00:04:15.046
McCormack.


00:04:15.179 --> 00:04:20.128
You know what NFL stands for?
"Not for long," pal. "Not for long."


00:04:20.809 --> 00:04:22.800
See you on the unemployment line.


00:04:22.978 --> 00:04:27.335
Hey, coach! Thanks for the three wins!
You're a bum!


00:04:27.941 --> 00:04:29.260
<i>A reminder, Eagles fans,</i>


00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:31.756
<i>to place your orders</i>
<i>for next year's season tickets.</i>


00:04:31.945 --> 00:04:33.219
Come on!


00:04:34.531 --> 00:04:36.328
Maybe next year, yeah?


00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:38.603
Yeah.


00:04:39.286 --> 00:04:41.516
Maybe we'll all be millionaires.


00:04:45.209 --> 00:04:48.360
Way to finish, guys.
Waited a whole season for this.


00:04:51.048 --> 00:04:53.608
- The worst team in the league!
- Losers!


00:04:55.552 --> 00:04:56.621
Go! Go!


00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:58.354
- Watch it. Watch out.
- Go! Go! Go!


00:04:58.514 --> 00:04:59.549
Watch out!


00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:06.007
- Jeez, Pete.
- Hey, ref, you better make that call.


00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:07.424
You all right?


00:05:11.652 --> 00:05:12.721
Hey!


00:05:12.861 --> 00:05:14.055
That's enough!


00:05:14.196 --> 00:05:15.265
- I said, come on!
- Come on.


00:05:15.406 --> 00:05:16.680
- Pete!
- Yeah!


00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:19.970
- Come on.
- You!


00:05:21.662 --> 00:05:22.697
I'm gonna kill that guy.


00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.060
Why don't you try
getting by him first, Pete?


00:05:25.249 --> 00:05:26.568
Why don't you shut your mouth?


00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:28.221
- Huddle up!
- Come on!


00:05:28.377 --> 00:05:30.493
- Hey, get in the huddle.
- Look who decided to show.


00:05:30.671 --> 00:05:32.309
Let's go. Huddle up! Huddle up!


00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:34.216
- Vincent!
- Yo, wait a minute.


00:05:34.383 --> 00:05:37.102
No way! Not him.
You don't show on time, you don't play!


00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:38.417
What's the matter, cuz?


00:05:38.554 --> 00:05:40.226
Afraid he's gonna
run all over you again?


00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:42.823
Would you shut up?
Let's play some football.


00:05:44.393 --> 00:05:45.587
What's up?


00:05:45.853 --> 00:05:48.208
- About time you got here.
- Sorry, guys.


00:05:49.064 --> 00:05:52.818
All right, let's do the one where Vince
kind of runs by everybody on one.


00:05:53.068 --> 00:05:54.137
- Ready?
- Here we go.


00:05:54.278 --> 00:05:55.393
Break!


00:05:56.238 --> 00:05:57.353
- Ready?
- Break!


00:05:57.489 --> 00:06:00.561
- Wanna tell me why you're late?
- My car's in a bad mood.


00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.343
- Watch the middle.
- Set!


00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:08.584
- Hut!
- Go! Go!


00:06:08.751 --> 00:06:10.264
Here we go! Here we go!


00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.714
- Here we go.
- Get him! Get him!


00:06:15.924 --> 00:06:17.596
Good hit. Yeah! Good hit.


00:06:18.093 --> 00:06:19.765
- You okay?
- Yeah, I'm good.


00:06:22.389 --> 00:06:23.788
Set! Hut!


00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:31.812
Fumble, fumble, fumble!
I got it! I got it! Yeah!


00:06:32.649 --> 00:06:34.082
- Break!
- Break!


00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:38.061
- I got one! I got one! I got one!
- You ain't got nothing.


00:06:44.078 --> 00:06:45.830
Set! Hut!


00:06:47.623 --> 00:06:50.012
Look out, Matt! Come on, look out!


00:07:02.638 --> 00:07:03.707
Hut!


00:07:08.477 --> 00:07:09.956
- Move it!
- Move! Move!


00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:12.170
Ball! Ball! Ball!


00:07:12.314 --> 00:07:13.713
I got it! I got it!


00:07:22.366 --> 00:07:24.197
- You all right?
- I'm all right.


00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.321
- Nice save, Vince.
- Thanks, man.


00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.655
Game over!


00:07:29.665 --> 00:07:31.178
Oh, man, my car!


00:07:31.792 --> 00:07:34.181
- Oh, yeah, huh?
- Pete!


00:07:34.378 --> 00:07:36.130
Right there, huh?
Remember that? Come on!


00:07:36.296 --> 00:07:38.810
- Pete, come on, cut it out.
- Did you see that?


00:07:39.007 --> 00:07:40.235
- We won.
- Come on, let's go.


00:07:40.384 --> 00:07:41.612
- You got money?
- Yeah.


00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.398
You better have money.


00:07:44.722 --> 00:07:45.757
Yeah!


00:07:49.643 --> 00:07:51.759
You look cold. Come a little closer.


00:08:05.075 --> 00:08:06.110
Hey.


00:08:12.207 --> 00:08:14.402
Come on, it was only for a few plays.


00:08:14.752 --> 00:08:16.185
That's great, Vince.


00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.059
We're out of work
and you're playing games.


00:08:19.423 --> 00:08:21.857
It's not like you couldn't use the time
for anything else, right?


00:08:22.051 --> 00:08:23.848
- Look, we're not out of work.
- Please.


00:08:24.011 --> 00:08:26.730
The school's giving you, what,
two days a week substitute teaching?


00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.249
You tend bar at night.


00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:31.223
What do you call that?
Gainfully employed?


00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.649
What do you want me to do?


00:08:38.817 --> 00:08:42.127
Look, things are gonna get better,
all right? I promise.


00:08:42.362 --> 00:08:45.399
When, Vince?
When are things gonna get better?


00:09:08.931 --> 00:09:10.603
- Hi, Mr Papale.
- Hi.


00:09:13.435 --> 00:09:16.188
So, the assignment was first act,
<i>Romeo and Juliet.</i>


00:09:16.647 --> 00:09:18.683
Oh, Mr Papale. May I help you?


00:09:19.775 --> 00:09:22.847
I'm sorry. Must be a mistake.
I thought this was my class.


00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.213
Hey, Mr Papale.


00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:28.814
Hey, guys.


00:09:28.951 --> 00:09:31.943
Mr Papale.
Can I have a word with you, please?


00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.090
We were trying to call you.


00:09:35.249 --> 00:09:37.763
Well, there was a mix-up with the bill
and they shut my phone off,


00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.632
but it should be back on today.


00:09:39.795 --> 00:09:43.583
We were calling you to let you know
that you won't be needed this summer.


00:09:43.924 --> 00:09:46.757
The district is forcing us
to make more cutbacks.


00:09:47.261 --> 00:09:50.378
And we have a lot of teachers
with more seniority than you.


00:09:51.974 --> 00:09:53.248
I'm sorry.


00:09:53.892 --> 00:09:55.723
I know it's a hell of a deal.


00:10:07.906 --> 00:10:09.862
<i>Well, it's no secret to anybody here</i>


00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:12.627
<i>that it's been a rough stretch</i>
<i>for the Eagles organisation.</i>


00:10:12.828 --> 00:10:15.023
<i>The last few seasons</i>
<i>haven't lived up to my expectations</i>


00:10:15.205 --> 00:10:18.481
<i>or to the expectations of the many fans</i>
<i>of this great team.</i>


00:10:18.709 --> 00:10:21.177
<i>But, gentlemen,</i>
<i>today, that is going to change.</i>


00:10:21.378 --> 00:10:23.687
<i>The man who's gonna bring us back</i>
<i>recently led UCLA</i>


00:10:23.881 --> 00:10:26.076
<i>to a Rose Bowl win over Ohio State.</i>


00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:28.169
<i>Please welcome Mr Dick Vermeil.</i>


00:10:28.844 --> 00:10:30.960
<i>Thank you, Mr Tose. Thank you.</i>


00:10:34.058 --> 00:10:36.572
<i>Well, I'd like to start by saying</i>
<i>what a tremendous honour it is</i>


00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:38.646
<i>to coach this particular football team...</i>


00:10:38.812 --> 00:10:41.326
- Think he brought his surfboard?
- <i>... and to coach in this city.</i>


00:10:41.523 --> 00:10:43.673
- Surfboard, Beach Boy records.
- <i>The Philadelphia Eagles</i>


00:10:43.859 --> 00:10:48.455
<i>have a very long and proud tradition</i>
<i>of winning and excellence.</i>


00:10:49.114 --> 00:10:51.833
<i>It's a tradition that's been lost</i>
<i>in recent years.</i>


00:10:52.493 --> 00:10:54.484
<i>It's a tradition</i>
<i>that I'm committed to restoring.</i>


00:10:54.661 --> 00:10:56.458
Man should be committed
for taking this job.


00:10:59.917 --> 00:11:01.111
Hey, Mick, you mean to tell me


00:11:01.251 --> 00:11:02.650
you didn't see that guy
clothesline Pete?


00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:05.309
- I didn't see nothing.
- I saw it from the car.


00:11:05.506 --> 00:11:08.066
Hey, that team had you guys beat
by a mile on that play.


00:11:08.258 --> 00:11:10.169
Oh, yeah? Then why aren't you
drinking over there?


00:11:10.344 --> 00:11:12.494
- Go to their bar, traitor.
- You want that on your tab?


00:11:12.679 --> 00:11:14.874
Hey, put a leash on that monkey.


00:11:15.349 --> 00:11:17.021
Vince, why does he get to run a tab,
I don't?


00:11:17.184 --> 00:11:19.493
Because he's got a job, that's why.


00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:24.255
That's great, Max. Yeah,
that's a great way to treat a friend.


00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:28.609
Hey, Max. Any chance I could pick up
a few more hours?


00:11:28.946 --> 00:11:30.299
- Sure. Why?
- <i>First up, let's bring in</i>


00:11:30.447 --> 00:11:32.483
<i>Wade Chambers</i>
<i>of Channel 11 Sports.</i>


00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:35.013
<i>Well, the Eagles took their time</i>
<i>on this one. But for the first time...</i>


00:11:35.202 --> 00:11:37.955
I'm giving my cousin from New York
a few hours starting Thursday.


00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:40.518
- You can have the rest if you want.
- Thanks. Appreciate it.


00:11:40.707 --> 00:11:44.461
<i>Owner Leonard Tose announced</i>
<i>the hiring of UCLA 's Dick Vermeil</i>


00:11:44.712 --> 00:11:46.270
- <i>as the Eagles' head coach.</i>
- Hey, Grumpy.


00:11:46.422 --> 00:11:47.980
You wanna turn up the tube?


00:11:48.132 --> 00:11:51.602
<i>... wasted no time before making</i>
<i>this surprising announcement.</i>


00:11:51.844 --> 00:11:55.120
<i>Before I take your questions,</i>
<i>I'd like to make a quick announcement.</i>


00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:59.465
<i>This coming Saturday,</i>
<i>at Veterans Stadium at 9:00 a.m.,</i>


00:11:59.727 --> 00:12:02.287
<i>the Philadelphia Eagles</i>
<i>will hold open tryouts.</i>


00:12:02.813 --> 00:12:04.565
- <i>We're open to all comers.</i>
- It's open.


00:12:04.732 --> 00:12:06.370
- This guy's out of his mind.
- <i>So we can go ahead</i>


00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:09.039
- <i>and start with the questions now.</i>
- <i>There you have it, Eagle fans.</i>


00:12:09.236 --> 00:12:11.796
<i>So strap on your helmets.</i>
<i>Throw on those shoulder pads.</i>


00:12:11.989 --> 00:12:14.298
<i>Here's your chance to play in the NFL.</i>


00:12:14.491 --> 00:12:16.846
I guess four wins
wasn't so bad after all.


00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:21.006
- Yo, Vince. What do you say?
- What?


00:12:21.248 --> 00:12:23.557
You're faster
than half those guys anyway.


00:12:24.168 --> 00:12:25.999
Hey, come on. Give it a shot.


00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:27.944
Yeah, Vince.


00:12:28.172 --> 00:12:29.651
Papale at the 40.


00:12:29.798 --> 00:12:32.073
At the 30. The 20.


00:12:32.259 --> 00:12:33.692
He's at the 10.


00:12:50.694 --> 00:12:51.809
Sharon!


00:12:59.119 --> 00:13:00.268
Sharon!


00:13:57.845 --> 00:14:00.962
- Hey.
- Hey. Sixteen-hour first day.


00:14:01.181 --> 00:14:04.298
- You're not going soft on me, are you?
- Look who's talking.


00:14:05.602 --> 00:14:07.081
Well, I found out today


00:14:07.229 --> 00:14:10.301
that there aren't any sprinkler systems
on the East Coast.


00:14:10.524 --> 00:14:13.914
Only took me a half an hour
to make that little discovery.


00:14:18.782 --> 00:14:20.534
You happen to see
that press conference today?


00:14:20.701 --> 00:14:22.931
Yeah. You looked good.


00:14:24.538 --> 00:14:27.177
The tryout come off
sounding a little desperate?


00:14:29.376 --> 00:14:30.855
Maybe a little.


00:14:34.548 --> 00:14:36.778
You don't seriously think
you're gonna find someone, do you?


00:14:36.967 --> 00:14:39.083
I'm just trying to get people excited,
that's all.


00:14:47.603 --> 00:14:50.595
So, Max just told me.
She took everything?


00:14:50.814 --> 00:14:53.772
- And she wants a divorce?
- Look, it's nothing, all right?


00:14:53.984 --> 00:14:55.895
Just forget about it, Tommy.


00:14:58.655 --> 00:15:02.170
Gin and tonic, light on the tonic,
and a Red neat for you, yeah?


00:15:02.409 --> 00:15:04.320
- That's right.
- Here you go.


00:15:04.495 --> 00:15:06.770
Sweetheart, if you could cook Italian,
I'd marry you.


00:15:06.955 --> 00:15:09.867
- Lf she had no legs, you'd marry her.
- Get out of here.


00:15:12.294 --> 00:15:14.762
- Sorry I'm late, Max.
- Hey, Vince, we're covered.


00:15:14.963 --> 00:15:17.682
- I know, I know, Max. I'm sorry.
- Hey, no problem.


00:15:18.008 --> 00:15:19.805
Anything you need, all right?


00:15:20.302 --> 00:15:23.374
Vince Papale,
meet my cousin, Janet Cantwell.


00:15:24.348 --> 00:15:27.499
- Hey.
- Nice to meet you.


00:15:28.352 --> 00:15:30.149
And just so everyone knows,


00:15:30.771 --> 00:15:32.250
we have a minor character flaw


00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:33.797
that we're all gonna
have to deal with here.


00:15:33.941 --> 00:15:36.375
- I don't see many flaws, Max.
- Watch it, Tommy.


00:15:36.568 --> 00:15:37.637
Hubba-hubba.


00:15:38.153 --> 00:15:40.587
My cousin, who is from New York,


00:15:40.781 --> 00:15:44.899
who was born in New York,
is a New York Giants fan.


00:15:45.911 --> 00:15:47.310
- Go, Giants.
- You gotta be kidding me.


00:15:47.454 --> 00:15:48.933
- A passionate New York Giants fan.
- Come on.


00:15:49.081 --> 00:15:50.116
Max, she's a Giant fan?


00:15:50.249 --> 00:15:52.001
- Maxie, come on.
- I know, I know.


00:15:52.167 --> 00:15:53.236
62-10.


00:15:53.377 --> 00:15:56.210
Giants humiliate the Eagles.
What was that? Three years ago?


00:15:56.422 --> 00:15:59.971
And we actually get our players
from something called the NFL draft.


00:16:00.968 --> 00:16:02.640
- Yeah!
- What kind of talk is that?


00:16:02.803 --> 00:16:03.838
See, Vince?


00:16:03.971 --> 00:16:06.405
That's another reason
why you gotta try out this weekend.


00:16:06.598 --> 00:16:08.748
- Nobody's trying out, Tommy, okay?
- Why not?


00:16:08.934 --> 00:16:11.050
You clean up at all our games.


00:16:11.228 --> 00:16:13.458
- He's 30 years old, for one thing.
- Oh, shut your mouth.


00:16:13.647 --> 00:16:15.638
Yeah, there's a little difference
between Mean Joe Greene


00:16:15.816 --> 00:16:17.215
and Bobby from the Tanker, you think?


00:16:17.359 --> 00:16:18.474
Hey, hey, screw Mean Joe.


00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:20.168
We don't even play Pittsburgh
this year.


00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:21.594
- Petey's right.
- Yeah, why not?


00:16:21.739 --> 00:16:23.855
Your old lady ain't gonna stop you.


00:16:24.575 --> 00:16:26.645
What? What'd you say, Johnny?


00:16:26.827 --> 00:16:27.942
- What?
- What do you mean, "What"?


00:16:28.078 --> 00:16:30.148
You playing stupid now?
You got a problem with me, Johnny?


00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:31.399
What'd I do?


00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.735
Why don't you get out of here, Johnny?


00:16:34.334 --> 00:16:35.767
Come on, right now.


00:16:44.303 --> 00:16:46.339
Hey, forget it. He's drunk.


00:16:47.097 --> 00:16:49.531
He just needs to find some work,
that's all.


00:17:18.253 --> 00:17:20.050
You know, you and your thing.


00:17:21.048 --> 00:17:23.482
Johnny losing it
'cause he can't pay a bill.


00:17:26.637 --> 00:17:27.911
Now, Pete...


00:17:28.639 --> 00:17:32.552
Pete ain't been right since his brother
Andrew came back dead from the war.


00:17:32.851 --> 00:17:35.160
What about you, Tommy?
You hanging in okay?


00:17:35.354 --> 00:17:36.582
Yeah, same old.


00:17:37.481 --> 00:17:40.041
Bunch of guys
talking about going on a strike.


00:17:40.776 --> 00:17:42.095
I ain't worried.


00:17:49.618 --> 00:17:52.337
You know I'm serious
about this tryout, right?


00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.440
Hey. I have, like, eight beers in me,


00:17:58.419 --> 00:18:00.569
but I'm serious, okay?


00:18:03.799 --> 00:18:05.755
Tommy, I mean,
I played one year of high school ball.


00:18:05.926 --> 00:18:06.961
It ain't gonna happen.


00:18:07.094 --> 00:18:09.654
There's no one I know that is
a bigger Eagle fan than you, okay?


00:18:09.847 --> 00:18:10.916
Nobody.


00:18:11.348 --> 00:18:13.782
All right, we're talking
about Veterans Stadium here.


00:18:13.976 --> 00:18:16.968
Where Eagles dare.
I mean, that is sacred ground, pally.


00:18:19.356 --> 00:18:21.824
Even if you're down there
for one hour, man,


00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:24.501
you're down there.


00:18:30.617 --> 00:18:32.972
Old Maxie's ready
to call it a night, huh?


00:18:34.663 --> 00:18:36.062
Last call, pally.


00:18:37.541 --> 00:18:39.020
Saddest music I know.


00:19:10.074 --> 00:19:12.872
- Hi, Pop.
- Vince.


00:19:16.455 --> 00:19:17.808
Come on in.


00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:28.228
I never did like her.


00:19:29.593 --> 00:19:31.390
I never told you that, did I?


00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.131
Guess maybe I should've
seen it coming, huh?


00:19:37.309 --> 00:19:38.378
What does she think?


00:19:38.519 --> 00:19:41.158
You're the only guy out there
trying to make ends meet?


00:19:42.856 --> 00:19:45.370
All those years,
your mother being sick...


00:19:49.113 --> 00:19:50.910
Well, that was nobody's fault.


00:19:54.034 --> 00:19:55.353
But this...


00:19:58.956 --> 00:20:01.311
Pop, I never had to ask you this before,


00:20:03.127 --> 00:20:05.482
but I'm gonna have trouble
making rent.


00:20:08.006 --> 00:20:09.041
Yeah.


00:20:11.093 --> 00:20:13.891
- How much you need?
- Hundred bucks.


00:20:14.346 --> 00:20:16.906
- I can pay you back as soon as I...
- No, no, forget it.


00:20:17.099 --> 00:20:19.329
There've been times
I've needed help, too.


00:20:19.518 --> 00:20:20.997
This is family.


00:20:21.812 --> 00:20:23.564
We've had some rough times,
you and me,


00:20:23.731 --> 00:20:25.608
but we stick on this one, okay?


00:20:28.193 --> 00:20:29.421
Thanks.


00:20:33.657 --> 00:20:36.091
So, what do you make
of this new coach?


00:20:38.704 --> 00:20:40.740
Beat Woody Hayes in the Rose Bowl.


00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.178
Saying something.


00:20:45.627 --> 00:20:48.664
You know, I heard from Maxie
that the guys are riding you pretty hard


00:20:48.881 --> 00:20:50.599
about going to this tryout.


00:20:51.675 --> 00:20:52.994
Yeah, well...


00:20:54.636 --> 00:20:56.228
You know, Vince,


00:20:56.889 --> 00:20:59.608
it might not be the worst thing
to let this one go.


00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.278
A man can only take so much failure.


00:21:15.949 --> 00:21:16.984
Hello, Philly fans.


00:21:17.117 --> 00:21:21.349
I'm here today with literally hundreds
of Eagle hopefuls waiting for their shot


00:21:21.622 --> 00:21:25.331
at coach Dick Vermeil's
much-publicised open tryout.


00:21:25.918 --> 00:21:27.192
Come on.


00:21:27.336 --> 00:21:28.928
Now, what brings you
out here today, sir?


00:21:29.088 --> 00:21:31.363
- Gonna be an Eagle, baby.
- Yeah!


00:21:34.259 --> 00:21:36.295
What makes you think
you have a chance out here?


00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:40.145
Well, Wade,
two years' high school football, varsity.


00:21:40.391 --> 00:21:41.460
Yeah!


00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.910
I'm 28 years old. Look at me.
I'm in the best shape of my life!


00:21:46.105 --> 00:21:48.016
Now, is there anything else
you'd like to say?


00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:49.384
Absolutely.


00:21:49.525 --> 00:21:55.202
<i>Fight, Eagles, fight</i>
<i>On the road to victory</i>


00:21:55.531 --> 00:21:57.567
<i>Fight, Eagles, fight</i>


00:21:57.741 --> 00:21:59.174
What more can I say?


00:22:00.119 --> 00:22:02.633
That's it. Looking for
some Philadelphia Eagles here.


00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:04.548
Lift your legs up. Okay.


00:22:07.126 --> 00:22:09.959
Go! Go! Come on. Move it. Move it.


00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:15.217
Come on. Hustle, hustle, hustle.


00:22:15.384 --> 00:22:16.783
Let's go. Four more.


00:22:17.553 --> 00:22:19.384
Come on. Hit it!


00:22:29.523 --> 00:22:30.797
All right. Beautiful. Let's do it.


00:22:30.941 --> 00:22:32.613
You know what?


00:22:32.901 --> 00:22:34.653
Forty-yard dash.
Move it. Move it. Let's go.


00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:36.219
Come on. Let's go, fellas. Do it.


00:22:36.363 --> 00:22:37.432
Come on, next group.


00:22:37.573 --> 00:22:39.404
Let's go, let's go, let's go.


00:22:40.033 --> 00:22:42.706
Move it. Move it.
Don't talk to him. Keep moving.


00:22:43.996 --> 00:22:45.429
Go, go, go, go!


00:22:46.498 --> 00:22:48.295
No, no, this is... This is too stupid.


00:22:48.459 --> 00:22:50.609
This is more stupid than I'm used to.


00:22:53.589 --> 00:22:56.945
Here we go. Next. Next.
Come on, get those knees up.


00:23:00.554 --> 00:23:02.226
- Thanks. Is this the updated list?
- Dick.


00:23:02.389 --> 00:23:04.380
- Yes, sir.
- Dick, this is brilliant.


00:23:04.558 --> 00:23:06.230
We haven't had
this many cameras here in 10 years.


00:23:06.393 --> 00:23:07.872
I want you to meet
three of your best players.


00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:09.612
We got Dean German.
Come here, guys. Come here.


00:23:09.772 --> 00:23:11.125
T.J. Banks. Ronnie Sampson.


00:23:11.273 --> 00:23:13.104
Say hello to Dick Vermeil,
your new coach.


00:23:13.275 --> 00:23:15.743
- How you doing, coach?
- Gentlemen.


00:23:15.944 --> 00:23:18.412
Mr Tose, Channel 8.
They want five minutes.


00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:21.309
Get over there. Run a sprint.


00:23:21.450 --> 00:23:23.441
Will somebody run a sprint
around here?


00:23:23.619 --> 00:23:25.098
You're a joke. You gotta be kidding me.


00:23:25.245 --> 00:23:28.282
So, how's it looking, coach?
Seeing anything yet?


00:23:29.083 --> 00:23:31.119
You're not worried, are you, T.J.?


00:23:31.585 --> 00:23:32.813
Should I be?


00:23:33.253 --> 00:23:36.165
Well, last year we had one
of the worst defences in the league.


00:23:36.382 --> 00:23:37.497
Offence wasn't much better.


00:23:37.633 --> 00:23:39.624
I'd say everybody needs to worry.


00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:42.152
See you boys at camp.


00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:46.403
We'll be there, coach.


00:23:47.184 --> 00:23:48.663
Longer than you will.


00:24:10.958 --> 00:24:12.676
Go, go, go, go.


00:24:15.713 --> 00:24:16.907
5.9.


00:24:17.256 --> 00:24:18.291
Let's go!


00:24:18.424 --> 00:24:19.459
- Gents.
- Coach.


00:24:19.591 --> 00:24:20.626
Hey.


00:24:20.759 --> 00:24:22.590
- Let's go.
- Come on, guys. Come on.


00:24:22.761 --> 00:24:24.035
6.4?


00:24:24.179 --> 00:24:26.056
Let's go, gentlemen. Find another gear.


00:24:26.223 --> 00:24:27.338
Go!


00:24:28.392 --> 00:24:31.145
They do know
they're supposed to be running, right?


00:24:31.395 --> 00:24:33.067
5.7. Next.


00:24:34.273 --> 00:24:35.342
You see?


00:24:35.482 --> 00:24:37.757
- How we doing?
- Get your head up. Let's go.


00:24:37.943 --> 00:24:40.059
I've seen glaciers move faster.


00:25:01.425 --> 00:25:02.744
Throw him a few.


00:25:32.206 --> 00:25:34.242
You gotta be kidding me
with these numbers, Dick.


00:25:34.416 --> 00:25:35.735
Can I please let these guys go?


00:25:35.876 --> 00:25:37.514
- Yeah, go on.
- Thank you.


00:25:41.548 --> 00:25:43.345
- That's it, gentlemen.
- Oh, that's it?


00:25:43.509 --> 00:25:45.101
- That's it?
- Thank you for coming out.


00:25:45.260 --> 00:25:47.933
- Whoa, whoa, coach!
- What do you mean, that's it?


00:25:49.098 --> 00:25:52.454
Good workout. Thanks for coming.
You worked real hard.


00:25:52.684 --> 00:25:54.959
Gotta work on your speed a little, okay?


00:26:28.762 --> 00:26:30.434
Great. Give me a break.


00:26:33.934 --> 00:26:36.323
How long you been
having trouble with this?


00:26:36.812 --> 00:26:38.165
Since I bought it.


00:26:38.772 --> 00:26:41.730
- I'm Dick Vermeil.
- Vince Papale.


00:26:42.276 --> 00:26:43.345
Vince.


00:26:43.777 --> 00:26:47.656
Pretty good workout you just turned in.
Any idea how fast you were running?


00:26:48.198 --> 00:26:50.871
- No, not really.
- That was a 4.5.


00:26:51.535 --> 00:26:54.971
This means you're a heck of a lot faster
than this car of yours.


00:26:56.165 --> 00:26:59.601
- Where'd you play your college ball?
- I didn't play college ball.


00:27:01.628 --> 00:27:04.062
Vince, you mind me
asking you how old you are?


00:27:04.256 --> 00:27:05.575
No, I don't mind.


00:27:06.133 --> 00:27:08.488
You mind me
asking how old you are, coach?


00:27:13.223 --> 00:27:15.054
- <i>Let's bring in Wade Chambers now...</i>
- Figure that one out.


00:27:15.225 --> 00:27:16.783
<i>... who spent most of his morning</i>
<i>at Veterans Stadium,</i>


00:27:16.935 --> 00:27:18.084
<i>watching Eagle hopefuls.</i>


00:27:18.228 --> 00:27:19.263
- Hey, buddy.
- Hey.


00:27:19.396 --> 00:27:21.830
<i>I guess we can call them hopefuls.</i>
<i>How'd it go out there this morning?</i>


00:27:22.024 --> 00:27:23.252
<i>It wasn't exactly a banner day...</i>


00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:25.038
You had a chance to go and didn't,
did you?


00:27:25.194 --> 00:27:26.752
<i>Former head coach Mike McCormack</i>


00:27:26.904 --> 00:27:28.895
<i>may not have run the tightest ship</i>
<i>in the NFL,</i>


00:27:29.073 --> 00:27:31.223
<i>but at least it wasn't a ship of fools.</i>


00:27:31.408 --> 00:27:33.683
- <i>Fight, Eagles, fight</i>
- Look at this.


00:27:33.869 --> 00:27:35.939
<i>On the road to victory</i>


00:27:36.121 --> 00:27:39.113
<i>That player, no surprise, did not get</i>
<i>an invitation to training camp.</i>


00:27:39.333 --> 00:27:40.402
<i>But believe it or not,</i>


00:27:40.542 --> 00:27:43.852
<i>new head coach Dick Vermeil</i>
<i>has decided to invite one person</i>


00:27:44.088 --> 00:27:45.919
<i>and one person only.</i>


00:27:46.090 --> 00:27:49.924
<i>He is Philadelphia native</i>
<i>Vince Papale...</i>


00:27:50.177 --> 00:27:51.246
What?


00:27:51.387 --> 00:27:53.184
<i>... a former teacher</i>
<i>who didn't even play college ball.</i>


00:27:53.347 --> 00:27:54.621
Oh, you must be kidding me!


00:27:54.765 --> 00:27:56.084
Congratulations!


00:28:00.562 --> 00:28:03.440
Next round's on the house
for my boy Vince here.


00:28:06.693 --> 00:28:07.808
I'll have another beer.


00:28:09.446 --> 00:28:12.882
Hey! I grew up with brothers,
but I got no problem hitting a girl.


00:28:14.535 --> 00:28:16.651
- She called Petey a girl.
- Vince!


00:28:17.204 --> 00:28:19.035
Yo, Vince,
she's disrespecting your team here.


00:28:19.206 --> 00:28:22.437
I'm not disrespecting his team.
I'm just respecting mine.


00:28:22.668 --> 00:28:25.580
All right, already, sweetheart.
You're such a Giants fan?


00:28:25.796 --> 00:28:28.947
- Name me a Giant. Any Giant.
- Any Giant?


00:28:29.174 --> 00:28:32.132
- Dangerous game, Johnny.
- I'm a dangerous guy.


00:28:32.344 --> 00:28:35.734
- Sam Huff.
- Everybody knows Sam Huff.


00:28:35.973 --> 00:28:38.407
Sam Huff.
All-American linebacker, West Virginia.


00:28:38.600 --> 00:28:41.273
Five years, All-Pro. Led the Giants
to the Championship Game


00:28:41.478 --> 00:28:45.073
in '56, '58, '59, '61, '62 and '63.


00:28:45.315 --> 00:28:47.351
Hey.
How many Championships they win?


00:28:47.526 --> 00:28:49.801
- Oh, shut up, Tommy.
- Oh, okay.


00:28:49.987 --> 00:28:51.022
The big goose egg.


00:28:51.155 --> 00:28:53.225
Oh, Ace wants to get into the game.


00:28:53.407 --> 00:28:56.365
All right, teach me something
about your beloved lggles.


00:28:56.577 --> 00:28:59.455
- That's easy. Tommy McDonald.
- Oh, that's Vince's boy.


00:29:00.414 --> 00:29:02.644
All-American wide receiver, Oklahoma.


00:29:03.083 --> 00:29:06.280
Led the Eagles to the Championship
in 1960 over Green Bay.


00:29:06.503 --> 00:29:07.538
1960.


00:29:07.671 --> 00:29:10.310
And who'd they beat to get there?
Yeah.


00:29:10.507 --> 00:29:13.226
The New York Giants!


00:29:14.261 --> 00:29:15.694
See, that's what I'm talking about.


00:29:15.846 --> 00:29:17.837
All right, everybody, quiet down.


00:29:20.184 --> 00:29:23.301
The last year or two we ain't had much
to raise our glasses to.


00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:24.953
- Yeah.
- You got that right.


00:29:25.105 --> 00:29:26.936
But we sure got something tonight,
don't we?


00:29:27.107 --> 00:29:28.222
Yeah.


00:29:33.197 --> 00:29:36.428
To Vince Papale, neighbourhood boy,


00:29:36.950 --> 00:29:39.589
who, starting two days from now,
will be on the field


00:29:39.787 --> 00:29:41.857
mixing it up with Bill Bergey.


00:29:42.039 --> 00:29:43.108
Bergey!


00:29:43.248 --> 00:29:44.397
T-Bone Parker.


00:29:44.541 --> 00:29:45.690
T-Bone!


00:29:45.834 --> 00:29:47.552
- Frankie LeMaster.
- Yeah!


00:29:47.711 --> 00:29:49.508
For that team we still love.


00:29:49.671 --> 00:29:50.740
Yeah!


00:29:50.881 --> 00:29:52.997
The Philadelphia Eagles!


00:30:16.281 --> 00:30:17.509
- You okay?
- Yeah.


00:30:17.658 --> 00:30:19.489
Let's go outside for a minute.


00:30:22.996 --> 00:30:24.270
Max, I'm all right.


00:30:24.415 --> 00:30:25.530
I already got some help. Don't worry.


00:30:25.666 --> 00:30:27.099
Yeah, well,
you're about to get some more.


00:30:27.251 --> 00:30:28.889
Come on.
Pay some bills while you're at camp.


00:30:29.044 --> 00:30:30.636
- Max.
- What?


00:30:30.796 --> 00:30:33.549
Look, it's not like
I'm gonna be making the team.


00:30:33.757 --> 00:30:35.270
Don't talk like that.


00:30:35.843 --> 00:30:38.835
You go out there and you play
like you're better than they are.


00:30:39.054 --> 00:30:40.612
- Come on.
- I'm gonna make it up to you, all right?


00:30:40.764 --> 00:30:42.402
Oh, you're damn right, you are.


00:30:42.558 --> 00:30:44.276
- Thanks, Max.
- All right.


00:30:44.435 --> 00:30:45.709
Hey.


00:30:45.853 --> 00:30:47.525
- Hey, you heading home?
- Yeah.


00:30:47.688 --> 00:30:50.282
One of you guys should get back
in there. It's getting crazy.


00:30:50.482 --> 00:30:51.631
- Animals.
- I got it.


00:30:51.775 --> 00:30:54.608
No, no, no. You should go home, too.
You're in training, remember?


00:30:54.820 --> 00:30:56.936
And walk her home while you're at it.
She's on your way.


00:30:57.114 --> 00:30:58.183
No, I'm fine.


00:30:58.323 --> 00:31:00.917
Right, and I'm gonna tell Uncle Richie
I let you walk home at night


00:31:01.118 --> 00:31:02.915
in South Philly wearing that?


00:31:03.078 --> 00:31:04.147
Come on.


00:31:06.040 --> 00:31:07.155
Good night.


00:31:07.458 --> 00:31:08.527
Whoa, whoa.


00:31:09.418 --> 00:31:11.568
Wait a second. Are you kidding me?


00:31:11.754 --> 00:31:13.984
Wade Chambers
right here at my place?


00:31:14.173 --> 00:31:15.367
Is this Max's?


00:31:15.549 --> 00:31:16.743
Yeah, it's Max's.


00:31:16.884 --> 00:31:18.954
Look at the... Max Cantwell.


00:31:19.136 --> 00:31:20.774
- This is my cousin, Janet.
- Hi.


00:31:20.929 --> 00:31:24.046
And this is the man you probably
wanna talk to, Vince Papale.


00:31:24.266 --> 00:31:25.335
Oh, no, thanks.


00:31:25.476 --> 00:31:27.307
People wanna know
who you are, Vince.


00:31:27.478 --> 00:31:28.797
All we need's five minutes.


00:31:28.937 --> 00:31:31.007
Hey, you could do it
right here outside my bar.


00:31:31.190 --> 00:31:34.580
- I gotta walk Janet home.
- Oh, no. I can wait.


00:31:37.696 --> 00:31:39.846
- All right, five minutes.
- All right.


00:31:41.617 --> 00:31:44.131
- Popoli or Papal?
- Papale.


00:31:45.162 --> 00:31:46.834
And all set.


00:31:47.331 --> 00:31:49.242
I'm here on Franklin Street
with Vince Papale,


00:31:49.416 --> 00:31:51.646
a bartender at Max's Bar and Grill


00:31:51.835 --> 00:31:53.712
and perhaps
future professional football player


00:31:53.879 --> 00:31:55.198
with the Philadelphia Eagles.


00:31:55.339 --> 00:31:56.408
Hey, whoa, whoa.


00:31:56.548 --> 00:31:58.823
So, Vince, tell us about your day
at Veterans Stadium.


00:31:59.009 --> 00:32:01.204
Hey, Pete!
What are you, a knucklehead?


00:32:01.387 --> 00:32:02.979
- All right, let's cut it.
- Going on my kegs?


00:32:03.138 --> 00:32:04.617
- Sorry.
- Come on, we're on TV here!


00:32:11.021 --> 00:32:13.057
So, how'd you become a Giants fan?


00:32:13.774 --> 00:32:16.049
Besides the fact
I was born in New York?


00:32:17.152 --> 00:32:20.269
Five brothers, all older.
Not much choice, yeah?


00:32:20.656 --> 00:32:22.248
That's why I like bartending.


00:32:22.408 --> 00:32:25.127
It's like I'm back home
listening to my brothers argue.


00:32:25.327 --> 00:32:26.806
You worked right there in the city?


00:32:26.954 --> 00:32:28.069
Yeah.


00:32:31.125 --> 00:32:33.559
So, you got something pretty big
happening here.


00:32:33.752 --> 00:32:36.186
I'll be right back here in a couple days.


00:32:38.757 --> 00:32:40.031
This is my place.


00:32:43.345 --> 00:32:45.063
Tommy McDonald, huh?


00:32:47.349 --> 00:32:48.782
I'll see you around?


00:33:09.038 --> 00:33:10.107
- Hello?
- <i>Hey.</i>


00:33:10.247 --> 00:33:13.683
Turn on Channel 11. They're gonna
do your interview in one minute.


00:33:26.889 --> 00:33:27.958
Vinnie.


00:33:28.098 --> 00:33:29.133
Pardon me, Mrs Spegnetti.


00:33:29.266 --> 00:33:32.258
Do you think maybe I could watch
your TV just for a few minutes?


00:33:32.978 --> 00:33:34.047
Okay.


00:33:34.188 --> 00:33:36.338
<i>Vince Papale, a part-time bartender,</i>


00:33:36.523 --> 00:33:39.242
<i>will be at Eagles training camp</i>
<i>in just two days.</i>


00:33:39.443 --> 00:33:42.241
- <i>This is no Tinseltown fairy tale, folks.</i>
- Vinnie, that's you on TV.


00:33:42.446 --> 00:33:45.563
<i>This is a real-life Cinderella story,</i>
<i>with a cleat instead of a slipper,</i>


00:33:45.783 --> 00:33:47.011
<i>right here in Philadelphia.</i>


00:33:47.159 --> 00:33:48.194
<i>Eagles, baby, Eagles!</i>


00:33:48.327 --> 00:33:50.079
- Oh, my God, my neighbour's famous.
- <i>Wade Chambers, Channel 11 News.</i>


00:33:50.788 --> 00:33:52.585
<i>Good luck, Vince.</i>
<i>We'll be pulling for you.</i>


00:33:52.748 --> 00:33:54.261
- <i>Don.</i>
- <i>Thanks, Wade.</i>


00:33:54.416 --> 00:33:56.407
<i>Certainly a different approach</i>
<i>being taken</i>


00:33:56.585 --> 00:33:58.576
<i>by new Eagles coach Dick Vermeil.</i>


00:33:59.088 --> 00:34:01.204
<i>In other news tonight,</i>
<i>a three-alarm fire broke out...</i>


00:34:01.382 --> 00:34:02.974
Change in game plan, coach?


00:34:03.133 --> 00:34:04.805
Just need to shake things up.


00:34:04.968 --> 00:34:06.640
If it means doing this
for a couple of weeks,


00:34:06.804 --> 00:34:08.203
might not be such a bad thing.


00:34:08.347 --> 00:34:09.860
Just be careful, Dick.


00:34:10.015 --> 00:34:11.653
This isn't UCLA anymore.


00:34:11.809 --> 00:34:13.925
These are the toughest fans there are.


00:34:14.103 --> 00:34:16.822
They threw snowballs at Santa Claus.
You remember?


00:34:20.734 --> 00:34:22.213
Gonna get some sleep?


00:34:23.987 --> 00:34:25.579
I'll sleep in December.


00:34:26.448 --> 00:34:27.676
Not if you make the playoffs.


00:36:17.726 --> 00:36:19.956
- Hey, Petey.
- Hey.


00:36:20.479 --> 00:36:22.868
- What are you doing here?
- Nothing.


00:36:23.065 --> 00:36:25.818
I was over at Mom's for dinner.
Sunday night, you know.


00:36:26.026 --> 00:36:27.459
Figured I'd just stop
and see if you was here.


00:36:27.611 --> 00:36:30.489
- You been here long?
- No, a few minutes is all.


00:36:33.409 --> 00:36:35.127
Your big day tomorrow, huh?


00:36:35.994 --> 00:36:38.747
I mean, I guess, you know?
See what happens.


00:36:40.582 --> 00:36:43.654
It's a good thing, Vinnie.
No matter how long it goes.


00:36:44.712 --> 00:36:46.464
Even if it's just for a day.


00:36:56.265 --> 00:37:00.019
I never said good luck to Andrew,
you know, before he left for Nam.


00:37:11.155 --> 00:37:12.907
You do good out there, okay?


00:37:35.345 --> 00:37:37.734
Just don't touch anything
that's not yours.


00:38:31.026 --> 00:38:32.095
Excuse me.


00:38:33.195 --> 00:38:34.833
My name's spelled wrong.


00:38:35.072 --> 00:38:38.860
Nothing personal, but by the time
I get to it, is it really gonna matter?


00:39:19.575 --> 00:39:20.724
Yeah. Come on.


00:39:20.868 --> 00:39:22.267
- What's up, Cool Breeze?
- All right?


00:39:22.411 --> 00:39:23.526
Hey, man.


00:39:23.662 --> 00:39:24.697
What's going on?


00:39:27.124 --> 00:39:29.035
- Oh, yeah.
- You deserve it, man.


00:39:29.251 --> 00:39:30.843
Gonna reach Harold Carmichael stats.


00:39:31.003 --> 00:39:32.755
- There ain't no way he's gonna do that.
- Hey, Carmichael.


00:39:32.921 --> 00:39:34.991
No, I was talking to Mom the other day.
Everything's good.


00:39:35.174 --> 00:39:36.289
Getting D.


00:39:42.097 --> 00:39:43.132
You ready for this?


00:39:43.265 --> 00:39:45.460
I'm probably gonna hit them hard
right out of the gate, A.C.


00:39:45.642 --> 00:39:46.757
See who's who.


00:39:46.894 --> 00:39:47.929
That's not what I meant.


00:39:48.062 --> 00:39:50.974
- Better be good, golden boy!
- Rookie coach.


00:39:51.190 --> 00:39:53.101
- This ain't college no more.
- You got one year, buddy.


00:39:53.275 --> 00:39:55.709
- You better be renting month-to-month!
- Welcome to the NFL.


00:39:55.903 --> 00:39:57.939
Gentlemen,
you're about to hear me say a word


00:39:58.113 --> 00:39:59.990
you'll never hear me say again.


00:40:00.908 --> 00:40:02.023
Lose.


00:40:03.869 --> 00:40:05.268
Means to fail.


00:40:06.455 --> 00:40:11.575
Means to be reduced,
to surrender, to relinquish.


00:40:13.003 --> 00:40:15.961
Over the years,
this team has surrendered.


00:40:16.173 --> 00:40:17.606
It's been reduced.


00:40:18.592 --> 00:40:20.071
This team has failed.


00:40:21.095 --> 00:40:22.164
No more.


00:40:23.472 --> 00:40:27.306
No more. Starting today,
we are on a path toward winning.


00:40:27.684 --> 00:40:30.073
And that's gonna require
a lot more work and sacrifice


00:40:30.270 --> 00:40:32.067
than many of you are used to.


00:40:32.231 --> 00:40:34.062
Six straight weeks of two-a-days.


00:40:34.233 --> 00:40:36.827
We'll go three,
three-and-a-half-hour sessions.


00:40:37.277 --> 00:40:39.837
We are gonna shake the rust
out of these shoulder pads


00:40:40.030 --> 00:40:41.941
and we're gonna become winners.


00:40:42.574 --> 00:40:44.530
And I don't care what your story is.


00:40:44.702 --> 00:40:48.536
Veteran, rookie, free agent. I don't care.


00:40:48.789 --> 00:40:51.940
You earn a spot on this team
by what you show me on this field.


00:40:52.167 --> 00:40:53.202
That's it.


00:40:54.336 --> 00:40:55.849
I play no favourites.


00:40:57.172 --> 00:40:58.241
None.


00:41:01.385 --> 00:41:03.501
All right. Let's go to work.


00:41:03.679 --> 00:41:07.228
One, two, three, two.
One, two, three, three.


00:41:07.474 --> 00:41:09.544
One, two, three, four.


00:41:09.727 --> 00:41:11.240
Work, work, work!


00:41:29.413 --> 00:41:30.482
Down!


00:41:36.670 --> 00:41:39.980
Get that helmet back on!
What do you think this is, a waltz?


00:41:40.215 --> 00:41:42.012
- Run it again.
- All right!


00:41:42.176 --> 00:41:43.495
- Do it again.
- You heard the man!


00:41:43.635 --> 00:41:45.114
We're doing it again!


00:41:47.848 --> 00:41:49.918
Bring it! Down! Get up!


00:41:54.188 --> 00:41:58.625
25, 26, 27, 28...


00:42:07.993 --> 00:42:09.790
Come on. Keep moving.


00:42:21.548 --> 00:42:23.300
Blue 99. Hut.


00:42:30.015 --> 00:42:31.733
Look at that white boy run!


00:42:33.102 --> 00:42:34.581
Thinks he's a football player!


00:42:34.728 --> 00:42:35.877
Hey, old man.


00:42:36.563 --> 00:42:38.042
This ain't high school!


00:42:38.190 --> 00:42:39.259
Hey, Banks!


00:42:39.483 --> 00:42:41.599
That old man just made you look bad.


00:42:43.404 --> 00:42:45.395
That's the way to finish, Papale!


00:42:56.750 --> 00:42:58.980
Stay on your feet or get off the field!


00:43:02.256 --> 00:43:03.325
Come on!


00:43:10.305 --> 00:43:11.533
Let's go, rook.


00:43:16.478 --> 00:43:17.797
Come on!


00:43:20.190 --> 00:43:21.225
Stay down!


00:43:21.358 --> 00:43:23.508
You gotta show me more than that, 83.


00:43:35.706 --> 00:43:36.855
I'll catch you later.


00:43:36.999 --> 00:43:38.876
- Next time, Stan.
- All right.


00:43:39.126 --> 00:43:42.436
Oh, dig! What do you think
you're doing out there, Pops?


00:43:42.671 --> 00:43:44.821
- What?
- It's the first day of camp.


00:43:45.215 --> 00:43:46.853
Might wanna settle down.


00:43:48.302 --> 00:43:51.658
Try helping out the ones who are
actually gonna make this team.


00:44:04.401 --> 00:44:06.039
- 442, Papale.
- Thanks.


00:44:06.195 --> 00:44:07.264
Dinner's at 7:00.


00:44:07.404 --> 00:44:08.757
Receivers' meeting at 9:00.


00:44:08.906 --> 00:44:10.385
Lights out, 11:00.


00:44:10.616 --> 00:44:11.685
Hey, coach.


00:44:12.326 --> 00:44:15.079
- Isn't there someone else in here?
- Not anymore.


00:44:29.718 --> 00:44:32.186
Hey, big guy. Come here for a second.


00:44:34.348 --> 00:44:35.417
Check this.


00:44:37.768 --> 00:44:39.406
She's cold-blooded, huh?


00:44:41.438 --> 00:44:42.757
Do you dig that?


00:45:09.717 --> 00:45:12.390
A Giants shirt? What, are you trying
to get me killed here?


00:45:12.594 --> 00:45:13.822
So how'd it go?


00:45:14.430 --> 00:45:16.785
I got a room.
Just haven't unpacked yet.


00:45:16.974 --> 00:45:18.453
I mean, it's a little different from playing


00:45:18.600 --> 00:45:20.192
with Maxie and the boys, though,
that's for sure.


00:45:20.352 --> 00:45:21.944
Well, I'll be sure to let them know that.


00:45:22.104 --> 00:45:23.981
Hey, you working tomorrow night?


00:45:24.148 --> 00:45:25.820
<i>I just thought maybe</i>
<i>if you weren't doing anything...</i>


00:45:25.983 --> 00:45:29.100
Not that we'd be, you know,
doing anything official, but...


00:45:30.904 --> 00:45:33.020
Well, being as you put it that way,


00:45:33.991 --> 00:45:35.504
<i>sure, yeah.</i>


00:45:35.659 --> 00:45:37.809
Great. Hey, and thanks
for the package, really.


00:45:37.995 --> 00:45:39.826
- No problem.
- All right, I'll call you tomorrow.


00:45:39.997 --> 00:45:41.191
<i>All right. Bye.</i>


00:45:44.334 --> 00:45:45.562
Take him down!


00:45:45.711 --> 00:45:46.860
Good job! Good job!


00:45:47.004 --> 00:45:48.562
She was right, old man!


00:45:48.756 --> 00:45:51.509
- You ain't going nowhere.
- That's right, German!


00:45:54.928 --> 00:45:55.963
Come here!


00:45:59.683 --> 00:46:02.834
- Hey!
- Hold on. That's enough! Break it up.


00:46:03.062 --> 00:46:04.461
- Come on!
- Back off!


00:46:05.189 --> 00:46:06.622
I said, back off!


00:46:07.024 --> 00:46:08.901
A.C., get them over to the sleds.


00:46:09.068 --> 00:46:10.979
All right, team. Let's move it.


00:46:11.153 --> 00:46:13.144
You heard the man. Let's move it.


00:46:14.114 --> 00:46:15.308
Move! Yeah!


00:46:16.825 --> 00:46:17.894
Game over!


00:46:21.288 --> 00:46:22.403
Philly, huh?


00:46:23.749 --> 00:46:25.102
I needed a change.


00:46:25.876 --> 00:46:27.992
A new city seemed like a good start.


00:46:31.423 --> 00:46:32.538
My ex.


00:46:32.674 --> 00:46:34.505
- Husband?
- Boyfriend.


00:46:36.512 --> 00:46:38.389
He wasn't what he said he was.


00:46:39.014 --> 00:46:40.527
What'd he say he was?


00:46:42.101 --> 00:46:43.216
Single.


00:46:45.854 --> 00:46:48.368
How about you?
If you don't mind me asking.


00:46:49.900 --> 00:46:51.618
Married five years.


00:46:52.319 --> 00:46:54.549
Showed up one day, she wasn't there.


00:46:56.365 --> 00:46:58.242
- Sorry.
- No, that's okay.


00:47:00.285 --> 00:47:02.116
So now you play football.


00:47:02.287 --> 00:47:04.164
Well, I've been playing
since I was a kid.


00:47:04.331 --> 00:47:05.844
Nothing big, you know.


00:47:06.291 --> 00:47:07.770
My mom was the one
that got me started.


00:47:07.918 --> 00:47:10.557
- Your mom?
- Yeah. Yeah, she was a great athlete.


00:47:10.754 --> 00:47:12.312
I mean, she got sick
when I was really young.


00:47:12.464 --> 00:47:14.500
Had a lot of medical problems.


00:47:15.384 --> 00:47:16.612
What about your dad?


00:47:16.760 --> 00:47:18.432
Well, he worked at the factory.


00:47:18.595 --> 00:47:20.267
I mean, he'd come home
as much as he could,


00:47:20.431 --> 00:47:22.103
but, you know, he had to pay the bills.


00:47:22.266 --> 00:47:25.622
I think her medical condition
really bothered him a lot, though.


00:47:26.979 --> 00:47:28.617
We always had the Eagles.


00:47:29.648 --> 00:47:32.208
You know, he'd love to tell
the story of Steve Van Buren.


00:47:32.401 --> 00:47:34.039
The '48 Championship Game?


00:47:37.406 --> 00:47:39.442
I have five brothers, remember?


00:47:39.700 --> 00:47:41.292
Yeah, I remember now.


00:47:41.452 --> 00:47:43.124
Anyway, I mean,
he'd talk about Steve Van Buren


00:47:43.287 --> 00:47:45.755
scoring the only touchdown
against the Chicago Cardinals,


00:47:45.956 --> 00:47:47.469
which won them the Championship.


00:47:47.624 --> 00:47:48.659
7-0.


00:47:49.543 --> 00:47:51.295
How do you know all of that?


00:48:00.387 --> 00:48:02.298
First cut's always the deepest.


00:48:09.730 --> 00:48:12.563
Coach wants to see you.
Bring your playbook.


00:48:20.866 --> 00:48:23.300
Coach wants to see you.
Bring your playbook.


00:48:27.247 --> 00:48:29.158
Bring your playbook.


00:48:51.939 --> 00:48:54.658
Coach wants to see you.
Bring your playbook.


00:49:15.838 --> 00:49:17.954
<i>Once again, the evening's top story.</i>


00:49:18.298 --> 00:49:21.495
<i>Union leaders are now calling</i>
<i>for a strike against Westinghouse.</i>


00:49:21.719 --> 00:49:23.835
<i>Two thousand workers</i>
<i>could be on the picket lines</i>


00:49:24.012 --> 00:49:25.889
<i>as early as tomorrow night.</i>


00:49:26.306 --> 00:49:28.695
<i>And now over to Wade Chambers</i>
<i>and sports.</i>


00:49:28.934 --> 00:49:31.323
<i>Well, the biggest news today</i>
<i>from Eagles training camp</i>


00:49:31.520 --> 00:49:35.911
<i>is that Philly's own Vince Papale</i>
<i>has made it past the first round of cuts.</i>


00:49:36.233 --> 00:49:38.906
<i>The part-time bartender remains</i>
<i>a long shot to make the team,</i>


00:49:39.111 --> 00:49:43.150
<i>but the mere fact that he's still around,</i>
<i>well, that's amazing in itself.</i>


00:49:43.991 --> 00:49:45.140
Attaboy, Vince.


00:49:45.284 --> 00:49:47.036
<i>Vermeil's coaching staff seems to be</i>
<i>focusing on defence this year.</i>


00:49:47.786 --> 00:49:49.822
Welcome to special teams, gentlemen.


00:49:49.997 --> 00:49:51.988
The only way that many of you
will make this roster


00:49:52.166 --> 00:49:54.122
is by proving yourself right here.


00:49:54.293 --> 00:49:56.966
To be successful,
you must throw away all fear.


00:49:57.880 --> 00:49:59.757
Speed and agility are critical,


00:49:59.923 --> 00:50:03.438
but desire and determination
are even more important.


00:50:03.677 --> 00:50:04.951
Ready.


00:50:09.183 --> 00:50:10.696
Move it, move it!


00:50:11.226 --> 00:50:12.341
That's it.


00:50:12.978 --> 00:50:14.491
- Got it.
- Way to go, Banks!


00:50:14.646 --> 00:50:16.125
Way to bring it home.


00:50:17.149 --> 00:50:18.298
- Looks good, right?
- Yeah.


00:50:18.442 --> 00:50:19.636
Next!


00:50:19.777 --> 00:50:21.210
Keep them on the 20.


00:50:28.744 --> 00:50:30.382
There you go, Sampson!


00:50:30.537 --> 00:50:32.767
That's what we're looking for out here!


00:50:34.249 --> 00:50:36.240
Cream's coming to the top now, Pops.


00:50:36.418 --> 00:50:38.249
- Give me some.
- Oh, yeah.


00:50:41.840 --> 00:50:42.909
What you doing in here?


00:50:43.050 --> 00:50:44.449
How am I supposed to run
in all this stuff?


00:50:44.593 --> 00:50:46.902
That stuff protects you.
It's there for a reason.


00:50:47.096 --> 00:50:48.449
You can't wear quarterback pads.


00:50:48.597 --> 00:50:50.110
You won't last a week wearing those.


00:50:50.265 --> 00:50:53.496
Nothing personal,
but is it really gonna matter?


00:50:57.356 --> 00:51:00.029
All right. Come on. You can do it!


00:51:01.026 --> 00:51:02.095
Ready.


00:52:07.092 --> 00:52:09.560
- What about Franks?
- They're beating him on the weak side.


00:52:09.762 --> 00:52:12.879
He better figure something out
if he wants to stick around.


00:53:15.953 --> 00:53:17.272
Chicken soup.


00:53:18.205 --> 00:53:19.763
Cures everything, yeah?


00:53:21.834 --> 00:53:24.667
- Tommy been in yet?
- Not so far.


00:53:27.297 --> 00:53:29.288
Anybody take you to Colombo's yet?


00:53:29.633 --> 00:53:31.589
The best cheese steak in Philly.


00:53:32.970 --> 00:53:34.244
Anybody asking?


00:53:35.305 --> 00:53:37.739
Well, if Maxie
don't have you working Friday.


00:53:38.934 --> 00:53:41.892
Long as 9:00 gets you back
for your curfew.


00:53:42.646 --> 00:53:43.681
All right.


00:53:48.402 --> 00:53:50.552
Hey, Rick, can you make me up
a grilled cheese?


00:53:50.738 --> 00:53:52.774
- Make it with fries.
- Oh, yeah.


00:53:53.699 --> 00:53:56.293
You're jumping back pretty fast,
huh, buddy boy?


00:53:58.495 --> 00:54:01.407
You really think a nice-looking girl
from New York's gonna come back,


00:54:01.623 --> 00:54:02.976
start over with one of us?


00:54:03.125 --> 00:54:06.515
Just 'cause everybody's
cheering for you trying to be an Eagle?


00:54:07.004 --> 00:54:09.837
We're just talking here.
What's your problem, Johnny?


00:54:10.883 --> 00:54:12.680
You'll still be nothing, man.


00:54:13.677 --> 00:54:16.714
When all this is over and done,
nothing.


00:54:17.639 --> 00:54:19.277
Just like the rest of us.


00:54:25.105 --> 00:54:26.902
Hey, Rick, can I get some more fries?


00:54:27.066 --> 00:54:28.260
Sure, why not?


00:54:56.804 --> 00:54:57.839
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:54:58.722 --> 00:55:01.316
So, this is the place, huh?
As good as it gets?


00:55:01.850 --> 00:55:03.283
Yeah. I mean, it's a little busy tonight.


00:55:03.435 --> 00:55:04.550
Yeah.


00:55:05.145 --> 00:55:07.454
Hey. You're Papale, right?


00:55:07.648 --> 00:55:08.717
Yeah.


00:55:08.857 --> 00:55:11.417
I don't care what anybody says.
You're doing a great job.


00:55:11.610 --> 00:55:13.282
- Thank you.
- Keep sticking it to those guys.


00:55:13.445 --> 00:55:14.958
- All right?
- All right.


00:55:16.657 --> 00:55:19.376
- Sorry about that.
- I guess you're still on the team, huh?


00:55:19.576 --> 00:55:22.249
Yeah, well,
there's a lot more cuts to go, but...


00:55:26.750 --> 00:55:27.785
What?


00:55:29.962 --> 00:55:31.873
I was just thinking, you know.


00:55:32.047 --> 00:55:35.596
I didn't think I was gonna make it
past the first week of all this,


00:55:35.843 --> 00:55:37.640
and now that I have, I mean...


00:55:37.803 --> 00:55:40.397
Well, maybe it's just better
if I just think about one thing


00:55:40.597 --> 00:55:42.315
instead of everything else.


00:55:43.142 --> 00:55:44.336
For right now.


00:55:45.144 --> 00:55:46.463
"Everything else"?


00:55:51.525 --> 00:55:53.914
Did you think
this was a date or something?


00:55:55.696 --> 00:55:59.848
Vince, I'm the last one
that wants to start something right now.


00:56:01.452 --> 00:56:04.728
Barely a month ago, I was
with the wrong guy, you were married.


00:56:04.955 --> 00:56:07.025
We're not exactly the perfect match.


00:56:07.207 --> 00:56:09.641
I didn't mean for it to sound like that.
That's not what I meant.


00:56:09.835 --> 00:56:11.632
No, you know,
Max thought it was gonna be busy


00:56:11.795 --> 00:56:13.513
at his place tonight, too,
so I'm gonna go over there


00:56:13.672 --> 00:56:14.991
and see if I can help him out.


00:56:15.132 --> 00:56:17.726
- Janet...
- No, we'll do this another night.


00:56:17.926 --> 00:56:19.917
I'll tell everyone you said hi.


00:56:44.161 --> 00:56:45.594
Denny Franks, right?


00:56:47.289 --> 00:56:48.688
Vermeil's trying to mix things up.


00:56:48.832 --> 00:56:51.141
He's putting rooks with veterans,
veterans with rooks.


00:56:51.335 --> 00:56:52.404
Crazy.


00:56:54.463 --> 00:56:56.135
So, are you like everyone else
around here?


00:56:56.298 --> 00:56:59.608
You mean, do I hate you? Yeah.
I'm a centre. I hate everybody.


00:57:01.011 --> 00:57:04.003
Yeah, well, your weak-side block,
it's not good enough.


00:57:08.811 --> 00:57:09.846
Says who?


00:57:09.978 --> 00:57:11.570
I heard some coaches talking...


00:57:11.730 --> 00:57:13.129
- What colour are my knuckles?
- What?


00:57:13.273 --> 00:57:14.501
What colour are my knuckles?


00:57:14.650 --> 00:57:15.719
- They're white.
- They're white.


00:57:15.859 --> 00:57:16.974
You see,
white 'cause my weight's forward.


00:57:17.111 --> 00:57:18.226
Means I'm coming after you.


00:57:18.362 --> 00:57:20.637
If I'm laying back,
the colour comes back.


00:57:24.284 --> 00:57:26.752
Tired of watching you
get hammered every day.


00:57:30.040 --> 00:57:31.393
I appreciate that.


00:57:32.042 --> 00:57:34.192
Is there anything else I should know?


00:57:34.378 --> 00:57:37.051
Yeah, lose the Giants shirt
hanging in my closet.


00:57:44.596 --> 00:57:46.154
You want a job? You want a job?
Let's go.


00:57:46.306 --> 00:57:48.774
- Let's go.
- Go, next group.


00:57:49.268 --> 00:57:51.304
- Set.
- Move it, move it, move it.


00:57:51.478 --> 00:57:54.914
Come on! All the way.
Touch the line! Touch the line!


00:57:55.941 --> 00:57:57.738
Let's go, let's go, let's go.


00:57:58.444 --> 00:58:01.277
Come on, gentlemen.
Let's act like you wanna be here!


00:58:02.156 --> 00:58:03.350
First group again.


00:58:03.490 --> 00:58:05.287
- All right, let's go. Let's go.
- Set.


00:58:05.451 --> 00:58:07.328
You heard him, first group.


00:58:07.494 --> 00:58:09.371
Right. All the way, all the way.


00:58:09.538 --> 00:58:10.687
Shake it off. Shake it off.


00:58:10.831 --> 00:58:13.709
Push through. That's good.
Push them through. Come on.


00:58:14.752 --> 00:58:16.743
You do know
we have a whole season in front of us?


00:58:16.920 --> 00:58:18.433
That's it.
Hit and release. Hit and release.


00:58:18.589 --> 00:58:20.307
Come on. Do it again. Do it again.


00:58:20.466 --> 00:58:22.696
We're still looking
for the last five players, right, A.C.?


00:58:22.885 --> 00:58:23.954
I know.


00:58:24.261 --> 00:58:26.536
But do we need to kill the first 40
to find the last five?


00:58:26.722 --> 00:58:29.680
Fred!
Nutcracker, other side of the field!


00:58:32.352 --> 00:58:33.626
Get in there.


00:58:37.399 --> 00:58:39.788
- Come on, rook.
- Put it on him, 57.


00:58:41.028 --> 00:58:42.780
- Come on, boy.
- Feel it. Come on.


00:58:42.946 --> 00:58:45.460
- Out of nowhere...
- You gotta feel it, Papale.


00:58:49.495 --> 00:58:51.929
- What are you doing?
- That's not quick enough, German.


00:58:52.122 --> 00:58:53.760
- Come on.
- Run it again. Now.


00:58:53.916 --> 00:58:55.429
- Let's go.
- Rook came to play today, man.


00:58:55.584 --> 00:58:57.222
German, he's about
to dial your number.


00:58:57.378 --> 00:58:58.857
Pastahead Papale!


00:58:59.046 --> 00:59:00.718
- Hey, German.
- German!


00:59:00.881 --> 00:59:02.155
- Go, German!
- Go!


00:59:02.883 --> 00:59:04.157
Get him, get him.


00:59:06.929 --> 00:59:09.124
Hey, 57, I don't know.
He's got your number, baby.


00:59:09.306 --> 00:59:10.421
Get up!


00:59:10.557 --> 00:59:11.672
Let's go.


00:59:12.059 --> 00:59:16.052
It ain't over. It ain't over. It ain't over.


00:59:17.898 --> 00:59:18.933
Come on.


00:59:19.483 --> 00:59:21.041
- Come on!
- Come on!


00:59:23.320 --> 00:59:25.276
- Set.
- Take that rookie down.


00:59:29.034 --> 00:59:31.867
- You showed him, German.
- Let's move them downstairs.


00:59:32.246 --> 00:59:34.714
- All right, gentlemen. Lower field.
- Yeah.


00:59:35.082 --> 00:59:36.197
Let's move.


00:59:36.959 --> 00:59:38.028
Let's go.


00:59:47.594 --> 00:59:49.630
All right, Vince. It's all right.


01:00:09.992 --> 01:00:12.950
<i>A less-than-perfect start</i>
<i>for new head coach Dick Vermeil,</i>


01:00:13.162 --> 01:00:15.357
<i>the Eagles losing</i>
<i>their preseason opener today</i>


01:00:15.539 --> 01:00:17.814
<i>to San Diego, 20-7.</i>


01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:20.468
<i>Still with the team,</i>
<i>for one more week, at least,</i>


01:00:20.669 --> 01:00:23.308
<i>South Philly's own favourite son,</i>
<i>Vince Papale.</i>


01:00:24.298 --> 01:00:26.050
- To Vinnie.
- Cheers, brother.


01:00:26.467 --> 01:00:28.105
<i>New week, same story.</i>


01:00:28.302 --> 01:00:30.452
<i>The Eagles,</i>
<i>losers of their opener a week ago,</i>


01:00:30.637 --> 01:00:32.434
<i>dropped their second straight</i>
<i>game today,</i>


01:00:32.598 --> 01:00:35.192
<i>a 14-7 decision to the Steelers.</i>


01:00:35.392 --> 01:00:39.101
<i>Well, let's just hope this isn't</i>
<i>the beginning of a long season, folks.</i>


01:00:39.855 --> 01:00:41.766
<i>If Dick Vermeil was hoping</i>
<i>for a honeymoon,</i>


01:00:41.940 --> 01:00:43.259
<i>he'll have to win a game first,</i>


01:00:43.400 --> 01:00:47.871
<i>Miami handing the Eagles their third</i>
<i>straight preseason loss today, 24</i>- <i>16.</i>


01:00:48.280 --> 01:00:49.349
Vinnie.


01:00:49.948 --> 01:00:51.779
<i>With final cuts only days away,</i>


01:00:51.950 --> 01:00:55.147
<i>South Philly's Vince Papale</i>
<i>saw a noticeable drop in playing time</i>


01:00:55.371 --> 01:00:59.159
<i>as the Eagles lose</i>
<i>to Cleveland tonight, 21</i>- <i>17,</i>


01:00:59.416 --> 01:01:02.374
<i>bringing their preseason record</i>
<i>to 0 and 6.</i>


01:01:28.070 --> 01:01:29.139
Vince.


01:01:30.030 --> 01:01:32.498
What brings you back
to the old neighbourhood?


01:01:32.825 --> 01:01:35.259
Don't you guys have kind of a curfew
out there?


01:01:35.452 --> 01:01:36.805
How you doing, Pop?


01:01:38.288 --> 01:01:39.323
You know.


01:01:44.378 --> 01:01:46.608
That was a hell of a time
to borrow money from you, Pop,


01:01:46.797 --> 01:01:48.389
with the strike and all.


01:01:48.632 --> 01:01:51.226
I talked to Maxie.
I'm gonna get my hours back.


01:01:51.552 --> 01:01:52.871
They let you go?


01:01:53.721 --> 01:01:54.836
No, not yet.


01:01:55.889 --> 01:01:57.641
They will, though, tomorrow.


01:01:59.226 --> 01:02:00.705
I've just been kidding myself, Pop.


01:02:00.853 --> 01:02:03.526
I mean, no one needs some hack
from South Philly.


01:02:03.897 --> 01:02:06.730
These guys are playing
the Dallas Cowboys on Sunday.


01:02:06.942 --> 01:02:09.251
Roger Staubach,
Ed Jones, Randy White.


01:02:10.738 --> 01:02:13.332
They need a football player.
They don't need me.


01:02:14.575 --> 01:02:15.849
Look, Vince...


01:02:15.993 --> 01:02:19.303
Look, it was gonna happen
sooner rather than later, Pop, right?


01:02:19.621 --> 01:02:21.976
I'm just tired of letting everybody down.


01:02:22.249 --> 01:02:24.001
You know, Sharon, the school.


01:02:24.168 --> 01:02:27.717
And everything that's going on
with you and Tommy and everybody.


01:02:28.255 --> 01:02:30.849
I mean, that's what's gonna
make tomorrow hard.


01:02:35.763 --> 01:02:36.878
You know how I used to tell you


01:02:37.014 --> 01:02:40.290
about Van Buren
scoring that touchdown back in '48?


01:02:40.684 --> 01:02:42.037
Yeah, I know.


01:02:42.978 --> 01:02:44.047
I know.


01:02:47.066 --> 01:02:51.344
That touchdown got me
through 30 years at that factory.


01:02:52.529 --> 01:02:55.407
Got me through all those times
your mother being sick.


01:02:59.244 --> 01:03:02.520
When I told you
not to get your hopes up,


01:03:04.917 --> 01:03:06.873
didn't mean that I wasn't.


01:03:08.629 --> 01:03:09.664
Okay?


01:03:30.609 --> 01:03:33.521
Okay, so we got one receiver slot open.


01:03:34.655 --> 01:03:36.486
It's either Sampson or Papale.


01:03:36.699 --> 01:03:38.894
Let's just go around the table.


01:03:39.660 --> 01:03:41.013
Sampson.


01:03:41.662 --> 01:03:43.095
Sampson.


01:03:45.499 --> 01:03:46.568
Sampson.


01:03:47.167 --> 01:03:49.556
But it's closer
than I thought it would be.


01:03:50.504 --> 01:03:51.732
Sampson.


01:04:01.014 --> 01:04:02.811
Your job's hard enough, Dick.


01:04:03.308 --> 01:04:06.186
Go with a guy like Papale next year,
once you've established yourself.


01:04:06.395 --> 01:04:09.865
You've got Mr Tose, the media,
everyone breathing down your neck.


01:04:10.399 --> 01:04:12.390
A good share of the veterans
don't even like him.


01:04:12.568 --> 01:04:13.796
He's got heart.


01:04:14.028 --> 01:04:16.781
People don't want heart, Dick.
They want wins.


01:04:26.123 --> 01:04:27.317
Knock, knock.


01:04:28.042 --> 01:04:29.760
- Hey.
- Remember us?


01:04:30.044 --> 01:04:31.159
Yes.


01:04:34.548 --> 01:04:35.742
I needed this.


01:04:36.467 --> 01:04:40.016
- Hey, Dad, can I try on the helmets?
- Yes. They're right over there.


01:04:40.262 --> 01:04:42.059
Put them back where you found them,
though, all right?


01:04:42.222 --> 01:04:43.291
Right.


01:04:44.099 --> 01:04:46.294
- They wanted to bring you dinner.
- Wow!


01:04:47.227 --> 01:04:48.501
I guess we're a little late.


01:04:48.645 --> 01:04:49.839
- No, I want it.
- No, I want it.


01:04:49.980 --> 01:04:51.971
No, this is great. This is great.


01:04:56.362 --> 01:04:59.513
- You look exhausted.
- Well, thank you.


01:05:00.991 --> 01:05:02.310
What's going on?


01:05:03.077 --> 01:05:04.396
No, we're just...


01:05:05.454 --> 01:05:07.809
We're thinking
about letting go of Papale.


01:05:08.207 --> 01:05:10.482
"We"? Isn't that your decision?


01:05:12.961 --> 01:05:14.758
This time it's a little different.


01:05:14.922 --> 01:05:17.959
But you said he was somebody
you could build a team around.


01:05:18.175 --> 01:05:21.053
Carol, there's a lot of other things
to consider here.


01:05:25.474 --> 01:05:28.864
What was it that you used to say
to your kids at Hillsdale High?


01:05:29.103 --> 01:05:31.856
That character is tested
when you're up against it?


01:05:32.481 --> 01:05:33.550
Yeah.


01:05:33.691 --> 01:05:36.967
And that's not the problem here.
He's got plenty of character.


01:05:37.194 --> 01:05:39.185
Who said I was talking about him?


01:05:52.543 --> 01:05:54.693
Papale, coach wants to see you.


01:05:57.047 --> 01:05:58.082
Hey.


01:05:59.967 --> 01:06:01.559
- About time he's out of here.
- Yeah.


01:06:01.719 --> 01:06:03.869
Got ourselves a roster. Hear that?


01:06:04.972 --> 01:06:06.246
Good times, baby.


01:06:11.186 --> 01:06:12.744
- Hey, coach.
- Hey, Vince.


01:06:12.896 --> 01:06:14.648
Come on in. Close the door.


01:06:24.950 --> 01:06:27.066
We haven't had much of a chance
to talk, have we?


01:06:27.244 --> 01:06:28.279
Not really.


01:06:30.831 --> 01:06:32.230
How you holding up?


01:06:32.499 --> 01:06:35.093
Well, couple bumps here and there,
nothing bad.


01:06:36.170 --> 01:06:38.730
So, how you doing, coach?
You hanging in okay?


01:06:41.508 --> 01:06:43.419
Couple of bumps here and there.


01:06:45.262 --> 01:06:46.297
I'm all right.


01:06:46.430 --> 01:06:49.103
It's not college, that's for sure.
Everything about it's a little...


01:06:49.308 --> 01:06:51.697
A little faster, little harder.


01:06:52.436 --> 01:06:54.074
I'm sure you can relate.


01:06:55.898 --> 01:06:59.368
Just wanna thank you for sticking
with me for this long, coach.


01:07:06.700 --> 01:07:09.453
Why don't you hang on to that
for a few more months?


01:07:16.085 --> 01:07:17.598
Welcome to the Eagles.


01:07:32.768 --> 01:07:35.999
When's the last time you've gone
two days without you needing a jump?


01:07:36.230 --> 01:07:38.585
- Sorry. I tried Pete.
- Are you kidding me?


01:07:39.692 --> 01:07:42.525
His car's worse than yours.
You'd both be stuck here.


01:07:45.030 --> 01:07:46.349
Your cable's good.


01:07:49.743 --> 01:07:51.495
Looks like you got a charge.


01:07:53.288 --> 01:07:55.722
Hey, buddy,
you sure this thing won't start?


01:07:58.961 --> 01:08:00.235
You kidding me?


01:08:03.257 --> 01:08:05.976
- You kidding with me right now?
- Nope.


01:08:08.679 --> 01:08:10.749
You're a freaking Eagle, aren't you?


01:08:11.181 --> 01:08:13.695
You're a freaking Philadelphia Eagle!


01:08:15.477 --> 01:08:18.514
- I wanted you to know first.
- This is huge.


01:08:18.856 --> 01:08:20.892
This is bigger than when
Tony Pantalano came back from Nam


01:08:21.066 --> 01:08:22.465
with the Bronze Star.


01:08:23.610 --> 01:08:24.929
Give me the keys.


01:08:25.946 --> 01:08:29.177
Let's go to Max's. You're buying.


01:08:30.159 --> 01:08:31.228
Hey.


01:08:31.368 --> 01:08:34.166
So, how you doing with the strike
and everything? You all right?


01:08:34.371 --> 01:08:35.520
I'm good now.


01:08:36.832 --> 01:08:37.947
I'm good now.


01:08:42.254 --> 01:08:44.131
Philadelphia Eagles!


01:08:44.673 --> 01:08:45.947
Yo, get in here!


01:08:47.760 --> 01:08:48.988
He's at the 40.


01:08:49.136 --> 01:08:51.366
- He's at the 30.
- Yo, look who it is. Yo!


01:08:51.555 --> 01:08:52.829
- He's at the 20.
- He's at the 20.


01:08:52.973 --> 01:08:58.366
Number 83, Vince Papale
of the Philadelphia Eagles!


01:09:01.148 --> 01:09:04.060
- My bartender, right here.
- Congratulations.


01:09:04.360 --> 01:09:06.237
I was gonna call you this week.


01:09:08.197 --> 01:09:11.633
E-A-G-L-E-S, Eagles!


01:09:13.744 --> 01:09:16.975
Yo! You!
Harold Carmichael, Bill Bergey.


01:09:17.206 --> 01:09:18.685
You're gonna be playing
with these guys.


01:09:18.832 --> 01:09:19.981
That's right.


01:09:20.626 --> 01:09:21.695
You did it.


01:09:24.296 --> 01:09:26.730
Your seats are gonna be
so much better than ours this year.


01:09:26.924 --> 01:09:28.801
Yeah, don't go giving mine away,
all right?


01:09:28.967 --> 01:09:30.719
I know where you're sitting.


01:09:33.097 --> 01:09:34.132
Kingie.


01:09:38.143 --> 01:09:40.532
- Hey, Pop.
- Come here.


01:09:42.022 --> 01:09:44.252
Stevie Van Buren's got nothing on you.


01:09:44.692 --> 01:09:46.330
Thanks, Pop.


01:09:46.485 --> 01:09:48.919
Maxie, line 'em up. It's my turn to buy.


01:10:00.249 --> 01:10:02.444
- From the Eagle's dad?
- From the Eagle.


01:10:14.888 --> 01:10:17.800
- Thanks, Maxie. Tonight was great.
- Forget it.


01:10:19.351 --> 01:10:22.661
There is something important
I wanna talk to you about, though.


01:10:23.313 --> 01:10:26.828
I've decided you can pay me back
anytime you want.


01:10:28.068 --> 01:10:29.183
First cheque.


01:10:30.654 --> 01:10:32.690
- I'm proud of you, Vince.
- Thanks.


01:10:33.782 --> 01:10:36.501
Let me ask you a question, Maxie.
About Johnny.


01:10:37.745 --> 01:10:41.533
He's scared, that's all.
Put yourself in his place.


01:10:42.124 --> 01:10:44.115
I don't even know what's going on,
you know, in his mind.


01:10:44.293 --> 01:10:46.727
I mean, he's been doing nothing
but riding me the past few weeks.


01:10:46.920 --> 01:10:48.069
Yeah, I know.


01:10:50.007 --> 01:10:51.838
He thinks you're gonna leave.


01:10:52.593 --> 01:10:54.151
This is the worst time in his life
right now.


01:10:54.303 --> 01:10:56.214
He's got no job. He's got no family.


01:10:56.388 --> 01:10:57.707
He's just got us.


01:10:58.640 --> 01:10:59.914
You're one of us.


01:11:01.018 --> 01:11:03.213
You know how it works in South Philly.


01:11:03.604 --> 01:11:06.038
Our strength has always been
in our numbers.


01:11:17.951 --> 01:11:19.145
Give it to me.


01:11:38.597 --> 01:11:40.872
That's right. Get your game face on.


01:12:04.915 --> 01:12:06.826
Must have been something I ate.


01:12:07.835 --> 01:12:10.224
Oh, yeah. Room service.


01:12:11.380 --> 01:12:12.529
Definitely.


01:12:23.475 --> 01:12:25.033
<i>Cowboy fans...</i>


01:12:40.617 --> 01:12:44.166
<i>Blue skies, 81 degrees,</i>
<i>a great day for the season opener.</i>


01:12:44.413 --> 01:12:46.449
- There he is.
- <i>No one's expecting miracles today,</i>


01:12:46.623 --> 01:12:48.659
<i>but all eyes will be</i>
<i>on coach Dick Vermeil's team</i>


01:12:48.834 --> 01:12:51.428
<i>as they take on</i>
<i>the defending NFC champions.</i>


01:12:56.508 --> 01:12:57.577
Come on.


01:13:11.148 --> 01:13:14.777
<i>And now the crowd welcomes</i>
<i>Tom Landry, NFC Coach of the Year.</i>


01:13:17.237 --> 01:13:19.193
Come on, guys. Come on. Come on.


01:13:24.286 --> 01:13:25.639
Philadelphia calls it.


01:13:25.788 --> 01:13:27.779
- Heads.
- Philadelphia calls heads.


01:13:29.041 --> 01:13:30.360
- Tails.
- We want the ball.


01:13:30.501 --> 01:13:32.332
- Dallas will receive.
- All right, kick team.


01:13:32.503 --> 01:13:33.572
Let's go.


01:13:36.673 --> 01:13:38.823
Bring it in here. Come on, come on.


01:13:39.009 --> 01:13:41.967
- Attack on three. One, two, three.
- Attack!


01:13:45.265 --> 01:13:46.414
Let's go win!


01:13:47.142 --> 01:13:48.814
Watch your outsides!


01:13:48.977 --> 01:13:52.049
Watch your lanes. Watch your lanes.


01:13:56.193 --> 01:13:58.832
- Go, Vinnie.
- All right, here we go.


01:13:59.029 --> 01:14:00.064
There he is.


01:14:05.828 --> 01:14:08.740
<i>And the first game</i>
<i>of the regular season is underway.</i>


01:14:30.352 --> 01:14:31.671
Let's go, defence!


01:14:38.569 --> 01:14:41.288
<i>Rookie Vince Papale</i>
<i>had an absolute bead on the runner,</i>


01:14:41.488 --> 01:14:43.877
<i>but he froze</i>
<i>like a deer in the headlights.</i>


01:14:44.575 --> 01:14:46.213
Oh, man, that wasn't good.


01:14:52.750 --> 01:14:54.820
All right, let's go, guys. Let's go.


01:14:55.044 --> 01:14:56.602
- Sorry, coach.
- You're sorry?


01:14:56.754 --> 01:14:58.346
I stuck my neck out for you.


01:14:58.505 --> 01:15:00.814
You start playing football
or you're gone.


01:15:08.265 --> 01:15:09.493
Losers!


01:15:21.779 --> 01:15:23.098
What happened, coach?


01:15:23.238 --> 01:15:24.717
- We missed the wedge.
- He froze.


01:15:24.865 --> 01:15:26.298
He got outside us.


01:15:31.830 --> 01:15:34.264
Blue 17. Set.


01:15:34.458 --> 01:15:35.652
Hut! Hut!


01:15:41.423 --> 01:15:42.981
Yeah. Yeah.


01:15:59.316 --> 01:16:01.989
We lose all six
of our preseason games, now this.


01:16:04.363 --> 01:16:05.478
0 and 7.


01:16:05.823 --> 01:16:08.462
It's not exactly
the direction I was hoping for.


01:16:19.503 --> 01:16:20.822
It'll get better. Come on.


01:16:20.963 --> 01:16:23.079
<i>Could be another long season,</i>
<i>Eagle fans.</i>


01:16:23.257 --> 01:16:25.930
<i>Not only was the team</i>
<i>no match at all for the Cowboys,</i>


01:16:26.135 --> 01:16:29.605
<i>but South Philly's Vince Papale</i>
<i>was a total bust in his pro debut.</i>


01:16:30.222 --> 01:16:32.531
<i>Coach Dick Vermeil's heart</i>
<i>may have been in the right place,</i>


01:16:32.725 --> 01:16:36.161
<i>but this team needs players right now,</i>
<i>not 30-year-old bartenders.</i>


01:17:09.928 --> 01:17:10.997
Hey.


01:17:11.847 --> 01:17:12.962
Hey.


01:17:13.557 --> 01:17:15.195
What are you doing here?


01:17:15.351 --> 01:17:16.989
I was just walking around.


01:17:19.897 --> 01:17:21.808
I needed to tell you something.


01:17:22.066 --> 01:17:24.864
- You know that night at Colombo's, I...
- You don't need to explain.


01:17:25.069 --> 01:17:26.468
I know, but please.


01:17:27.905 --> 01:17:30.897
It wasn't that I was just thinking
about that one thing.


01:17:31.742 --> 01:17:34.461
I was just scared because
I knew the way I could feel about you,


01:17:34.661 --> 01:17:37.016
and it was just too soon.
At least for me.


01:17:39.249 --> 01:17:41.365
I don't know what's gonna happen
with all this.


01:17:41.543 --> 01:17:43.693
Even if I never got to see you again,


01:17:44.213 --> 01:17:46.932
you go off, you get married,
you have five kids,


01:17:49.593 --> 01:17:51.948
I just wanted to let you know how I felt.


01:17:55.099 --> 01:17:56.327
I can't, Vince.


